{"entryType":"UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)","primaryAccession":"O33407","secondaryAccessions":["Q7DC45","Q9F3Y2"],"uniProtkbId":"ESTA_PSEAE","entryAudit":{"firstPublicDate":"2004-12-21","lastAnnotationUpdateDate":"2026-06-10","lastSequenceUpdateDate":"1998-01-01","entryVersion":151,"sequenceVersion":1},"annotationScore":5.0,"organism":{"scientificName":"Pseudomonas aeruginosa (strain ATCC 15692 / DSM 22644 / CIP 104116 / JCM 14847 / LMG 12228 / 1C / PRS 101 / PAO1)","taxonId":208964,"lineage":["Bacteria","Pseudomonadati","Pseudomonadota","Gammaproteobacteria","Pseudomonadales","Pseudomonadaceae","Pseudomonas"]},"proteinExistence":"1: Evidence at protein level","proteinDescription":{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"value":"Esterase EstA"},"ecNumbers":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"10559163"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"20931591"}],"value":"3.1.1.1"}]},"alternativeNames":[{"fullName":{"value":"Autotransporter esterase EstA"}}],"flag":"Precursor"},"genes":[{"geneName":{"value":"estA"},"synonyms":[{"value":"papA"}],"orderedLocusNames":[{"value":"PA5112"}]}],"comments":[{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"17631636"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"20931591"}],"value":"Esterase whose enzymatic activity is required for rhamnolipid production, all kinds of cell motility (swimming, swarming, and twitching), and biofilm formation; the exact role of EstA in these processes is unclear. In vitro, has pronounced esterase activities towards p-nitrophenyl esters of short acyl chain length (C4-C6) and Tween detergents. Also shows relatively high activity towards beta-naphthyl butyrate, whereas its activities towards triacylglycerols and acyls-CoA are negligible"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"commentType":"CATALYTIC ACTIVITY","reaction":{"name":"a carboxylic ester + H2O = an alcohol + a carboxylate + H(+)","reactionCrossReferences":[{"database":"Rhea","id"